Btw this is how you build Macports on your local machine. The idea is to have multiple such installations all operating w/o root privileges
./configure --with-no-root-privileges --prefix=/Users/kutty_banerjee/bin/macports 


=------
/etc/macports/macports.conf
  buildfromsource <use this option>
  build_arch


-------
port installed requested
  This will give you the list of Ports you installed (vs dependencies installed)

-------
port -v selfupdate     // to install the latest version of ports
port upgrade outdated  // to install the latest version of everything
-------
port uninstall leaves  // Get rid of unused packages
port list inactive     // name says it all, keep this in mind but the few times I tried it
     	  	       // it didn't do the right thing. Listed ports that I knew I was 
		       // using and that too, their latest versions

-------
port install boost build.jobs=10  // This will use parallel make and pass that number
// You can also control it in etc/macports/macports.conf buildmakejobs=n
